    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d256">

                <pb facs="0505" n="495" xml:id="pg495"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Marshall Mission Files, Lot 54–D270</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by General Chou
                            En-lai to General Marshall
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1946-11-08">November 8,
                        1946</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>With reference to my memorandum under date of October 9th<anchor n="85"
                        xml:id="d256-f1"/> which I requested to be transmitted to the Generalissimo,
                    I have not as yet received a reply.</p>
                <p>As regards the Generalissimo’s statement of October 16th, I have already on
                    October 17th explained the Communist attitude and views to the Government
                    representatives, Wu Teh Chen, Shao Li Tze<anchor n="86" xml:id="d256-f2"/> and
                    Lei cheng<anchor n="87" xml:id="d256-f3"/> in Shanghai. I also explained the
                    same to the Third Party Group on October 18th. On the same day, I received a
                    copy of Generalissimo’s memorandum to you under date of October 17th<anchor
                        n="88" xml:id="d256-f4"/> which was forwarded to me from your office. On
                    return to Nanking I thereupon immediately explained our views to you and Dr.
                    Stuart and I presume that you are familiar with those.</p>
                <p>Since returning to Nanking all the negotiations were conducted through the Third
                    Party. Through their good offices there is some possibility for the reconvening
                    of the Committee of Three, the PCC Steering Committee and the Draft Reviewing
                    Committee and we are still exerting efforts for this end.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chou En-lai</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
